{"id":"pantheon-q188856","name":"Panthéon","qid":"Q188856","country":"France","locality":"5th arrondissement of Paris, Quartier de la Sorbonne","lat":"48.846198","lon":"2.3461054","built":"1758","year":1758,"year_text":"1758","century":"18th century","era":"Early modern","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"Neoclassical architecture","heritage":"classified historical monument","type":"church building; mausoleum","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panthéon","text":"The Panthéon (French: [pɑ̃.te.ɔ̃], from Ancient Greek πάνθειον (pántheion) '[temple] to all the gods') is a monument in the 5th arrondissement of Paris, France. It stands in the Latin Quarter (Quartier Latin), on the Montagne Sainte-Geneviève, in the centre of the Place du Panthéon, which was named after it. The edifice was built between 1758 and 1790, from designs by Jacques-Germain Soufflot, at the behest of King Louis XV; the king intended it as a church dedicated to Saint Genevieve, Paris's patron saint, whose relics were to be housed in the church.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panth%C3%A9on","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-2b2303fc6b0b","w":1200,"h":900,"title":"Night Paris.jpg","o":"gh-2b2303fc6b0b.jpg","credit":{"text":"Prosthetic Head","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Night_Paris.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-6782134caa9a","w":1200,"h":815,"title":"Panthéon, Paris 25 March 2012.jpg","o":"gh-6782134caa9a.jpg","credit":{"text":"Camille Gévaudan","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panth%C3%A9on%2C_Paris_25_March_2012.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-c99584e0c896","w":1200,"h":801,"title":"Inside the Pantheon, Paris France (4198912183).jpg","o":"gh-c99584e0c896.jpg","credit":{"text":"Alex Proimos from Sydney, Australia","license":"CC BY 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inside_the_Pantheon%2C_Paris_France_%284198912183%29.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"the-saboteur--pantheon","game":"the-saboteur","name":"Pantheon","verified":false,"text":"The Panthéon (French: Le Panthéon) is a famous monument in The Saboteur, that serves as a heavily-armed Nazi stronghold.","text_source":"https://thesaboteur.fandom.com/wiki/Pantheon","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-2f14c5278ef6","w":1200,"h":750,"o":"gh-2f14c5278ef6.webp","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from The Saboteur, © Electronic Arts.","source":"https://thesaboteur.fandom.com/wiki/File:Saboteur_2015-01-25_21-39-06-71.png","via":"Fandom (thesaboteur)","note":"Fandom upload by UnknownToaster on 2015-01-26"}},{"id":"gh-6617f2c8e15b","w":1200,"h":750,"o":"gh-6617f2c8e15b.webp","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from The Saboteur, © Electronic Arts.","source":"https://thesaboteur.fandom.com/wiki/File:Saboteur_2015-01-25_21-23-41-34.png","via":"Fandom (thesaboteur)","note":"Fandom upload by UnknownToaster on 2015-01-26"}},{"id":"gh-8bfde429f597","w":1024,"h":768,"o":"gh-8bfde429f597.webp","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from The Saboteur, © Electronic Arts.","source":"https://thesaboteur.fandom.com/wiki/File:Saboteur_2014-11-07_18-09-22-14.png","via":"Fandom (thesaboteur)","note":"Fandom upload by UnknownToaster on 2015-01-26"}},{"id":"gh-96699bf9c5a9","w":1200,"h":750,"o":"gh-96699bf9c5a9.webp","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from The Saboteur, © Electronic Arts.","source":"https://thesaboteur.fandom.com/wiki/File:Saboteur_2015-01-25_21-34-17-88.png","via":"Fandom (thesaboteur)","note":"Fandom upload by UnknownToaster on 2015-01-26"}},{"id":"gh-a2059f88e205","w":1200,"h":750,"o":"gh-a2059f88e205.webp","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from The Saboteur, © Electronic Arts.","source":"https://thesaboteur.fandom.com/wiki/File:Saboteur_2015-01-